WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.000
On December 13th,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.904
U.S. prosecutors charged FTX founder

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.510
Sam Bankman-Fried with eight counts of fraud and conspiracy.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.440
I think it's fair to say that by anyone's life,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.420
this is one of the biggest financial frauds in American history.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.980
The charges were announced amid a series of events playing out across two countries

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.430
that also included an arrest in the Bahamas,

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:27.022
a criminal indictment, and a congressional hearing on the crypto exchange's sudden demise.

00:00:29.023 --> 00:00:31.620
Bahamian police said they took Bankman-Fried into custody

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.300
at his apartment in Nassau on December 12th for charges of various financial 

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.660
offenses against laws of the United States,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.734
which are also offenses against laws of the Commonwealth of the Bahamas.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:46.320
Authorities said the arrest was made based on an indictment filed by the 

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.230
U.S. Attorney's Office for the Southern District of New York.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:53.920
Bankman-Fried and his co-conspirators stole billions of dollars from FTX customers.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.147
The indictment accuses Bankman-Fried of misappropriating FTX.com

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.720
customers' deposits and using those to pay expenses and debts of 

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.053
Alameda Research, his crypto hedge fund.

00:01:06.053 --> 00:01:08.250
Since FTX filed for bankruptcy in November.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.950
Bankman-Fried has said in multiple interviews that he bore responsibility for the company's collapse,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.160
but he did not knowingly commit any fraud.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.440
I was trying to do the best I could. Obviously, that wasn't nearly as good as I thought it was.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:26.469
Bankman-Fried is reviewing the charges with his legal team and considering all of his legal options, his lawyer said.

00:01:26.469 --> 00:01:31.139
Also on December 13th, the Securities and Exchange Commission alleged

00:01:31.139 --> 00:01:37.745
in a civil lawsuit that Bankman-Fried diverted customer funds from the start of FTX to support Alameda.

00:01:37.745 --> 00:01:41.900
The SEC says that while he spent lavishly on office space and condominiums in the 

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.260
Bahamas and sank billions of dollars of customer funds into speculative venture 

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.170
investments,

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.980
Bankman-Fried's house of cards began to crumble.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:54.825
His brazen multiyear scheme finally came to an end when FTX,

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:01.563
Alameda and their tangled web of affiliates filed for bankruptcy on November 11, 2022.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.167
That collapse has had far-reaching consequences for FTX customers,

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.840
for its investors, and for its counter parties.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.371
The Commodity Futures Trading Commission,

00:02:11.371 --> 00:02:16.950
another U.S. markets regulator, filed a separate lawsuit on the same day linking his alleged fraudulent

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:22.013
conduct at Alameda and FTX to markets that the CFTC regulates.

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:24.110
The complaints are the latest twist in a 

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:29.686
saga that has rattled the world of cryptocurrencies and has caught the attention of U.S. lawmakers.

00:02:29.686 --> 00:02:33.050
Rest assured that this committee will not stop

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.592
until we uncover the full truth behind the collapse of FTX.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.560
At a congressional hearing in Washington,

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.730
FTX's new chief executive told lawmakers that the company has incurred losses in excess of 

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.230
$7 billion.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.290
This isn't this isn't Uh you know,

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:52.671
sophisticated whatsoever. This is just plain old embezzlement.

00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:55.040
Hours after the criminal indictment was unsealed,

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.420
a magistrate judge in the Bahamas denied bail

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:03.679
to Bankman-Fried and said he should be remanded to Bahamian custody until February 8, 2023.

